Astrodactyl's body generates green internalized stellar energy,{{Refn|[[:File:Astrodactyl Internalized Star Power.png]]|group = DJW|name = Archive}}{{Refn|Alternate versions of Astrodactyl are shown possessing star power in different colors. For example, [[Weapon XI (Present)|17-year-old Mutant Kevin]]'s star power is colored red.<ref>''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]''</ref>|group = note}} which he can weaponize by shooting it out of his mouth,<ref name="AFoB" /> or alternatively channeling it through the holes on his arms.<ref name="WYWA">''[[While You Were Away]]''</ref> Astrodactyl has the power of dynakinesis, meaning that he can influence the direction and form of the energy that's released from his body with extreme precision. Using this power, Astrodactyl is capable of creating constructs made from stellar energy,{{Refn|group = DJW|name = Archive}} such as whips<ref name="WYWA" /> or throwing stars.{{Refn|[[:File:Astrodactyl Stars.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Astrodactyl has a natural jetpack attached to his back, which his internalized energy extends to, allowing him to fly at incredible speeds. While soaring through the sky, he can use his jetpack to form waves of energy that explode on contact.<ref name="WYWA" /> These waves are strong enough to instantly knock an [[Incursean Space Fighter]] out of the air.<ref>''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]''</ref> Futhermore, Astrodactyl has wings he can fold out at will.<ref name="WYWA" />

Astrodactyl is strong enough to carry [[Human (Classic)|Humans]] while flying,<ref name="ATTWN">''[[And Then There Were None]]''</ref> free himself from adhesive traps powerful enough to trap [[Revonnahgander]]s,<ref name="CT">''[[Collect This]]''</ref> tear apart [[Thep Khufan]]'s tendrils,<ref name="ATTWN" /> as well as swing around [[Techadon Robot]]s using his whips with enough force to burst a brick wall.<ref name="C5">''[[Clyde 5]]''</ref> During the aforementioned confrontation, he has also demonstrated enhanced reflexes by dodging lasers. He can also perform acrobatic techniques.<ref name="C5" /> His strength also extends to his feet, allowing him to lift creatures larger than him, such as [[Cerebrocrustacean]]s.<ref name="AFoB" />

Astrodactyl is very durable, being able to survive crashing onto the ground from several hundreds of feet in the sky.<ref name="CT" /> Astrodactyl can also survive in the vacuum of space.

==Weaknesses==
[[File:UPdC (436).png|thumb|Electricity Vulnerability]]
Astrodactyl is vulnerable to electricity, such as that generated by a Cerebrocrustacean.<ref name="AFoB" />

==History==
===Omniverse===
*Astrodactyl first appeared in ''[[While You Were Away]]'', where he battled [[Dr. Psychobos]] and helped destroy the supply of [[Amber Ogia]].{{Refn|Astrodactyl was never locked in the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]].{{Refn|[[:File:New Aliens in OV Weren't Locked.png]]|group = DJW}}|group = note}}
*In ''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]'', Astrodactyl battled the [[Incursean]]s before the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]]'s randomizer function made him switch into [[Snare-Oh]].
*In ''[[Mud is Thicker Than Water]]'', Astrodactyl battled [[Psyphon]] and [[Psyphon's Gang|his gang]].
*In ''[[A Fistful of Brains]]'', Astrodactyl escaped from [[Khyber]]'s hunting grounds and briefly fought [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Brainstorm]] until they both reverted.
*In ''[[The Vampire Strikes Back]]'', Astrodactyl flew back to [[Anur Transyl]] after [[Rad Dudesman|Rad]] ejected him from the [[Lovely Duck]].
*In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', Astrodactyl battled [[Bad Ben|Bad]] [[Gravattack]] and saved [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] from [[Eon]].
*In ''[[Collect This]]'', Astrodactyl freed himself and [[Rook Blonko|Rook]] before going after [[Collectimus]].
*In ''[[Clyde 5]]'', Astrodactyl chased after [[Clyde Fife|Clyde]] and battled some [[Techadon Robot]]s.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Astrodactyl appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

